      "content": "<h3>All Vector methods at a glance</h3>\n<p><em>n</em> is the number of elements. The first group is the classic Vector API; the second is the List API that Vector shares with ArrayList.</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\n<tr><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Method</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">What it does</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Time</th></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>addElement(e)</strong></td><td>Adds at the end (old name of add)</td><td>O(1) amortised</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>insertElementAt(e, i)</strong></td><td>Inserts at index i</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>elementAt(i)</strong> / <strong>firstElement()</strong> / <strong>lastElement()</strong></td><td>Reads by index / first / last</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>setElementAt(e, i)</strong></td><td>Replaces the element at i</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>removeElement(o)</strong> / <strong>removeElementAt(i)</strong> / <strong>removeAllElements()</strong></td><td>Removes by value / index / everything</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>capacity()</strong> / <strong>ensureCapacity(n)</strong> / <strong>trimToSize()</strong> / <strong>setSize(n)</strong></td><td>Capacity management (setSize pads with null or truncates)</td><td>O(1) / O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>elements()</strong></td><td>An old-style Enumeration (not fail-fast)</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>copyInto(Object[])</strong></td><td>Copies the elements into an array</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>indexOf(o, from)</strong> / <strong>lastIndexOf(o, from)</strong></td><td>Search starting at a given index</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>add, get, set, remove, contains, size, clear, addAll, removeAll, retainAll ...</strong></td><td>The ordinary List methods, all synchronized</td><td>as ArrayList</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>sort, forEach, removeIf, replaceAll, stream, subList, iterator, listIterator</strong></td><td>Inherited List helpers</td><td>as ArrayList</td></tr>\n</table>"
